/target
# `.github/scripts/deny-wrappers.py` is the only Python here, and running it leaves
# nothing — but *importing* it, as its own mutation testing does, writes a `.pyc` beside
# it, which `git add -A` would then commit.
__pycache__/
/CLAUDE.local.md
/local/
/.git-commit-msg
/.env
# Agent scratch: worktrees, and the throwaway scripts written beside them. Narrowed to
# `/.claude/` and not `.claude/` so a crate of that name would still be tracked. A bare
# `git add -A` swept a local tool in here twice during #333 before this line existed.
/.claude/
